WEBVTT

00:28:59.958 --> 00:29:04.518
between long-term global need
and short-term interest,

00:29:04.542 --> 00:29:07.434
they will go with the short-term interest.

00:29:07.458 --> 00:29:09.809
So don't pit those two things
against each other.

00:29:09.833 --> 00:29:14.768
That is by definition a battle
that you have lost from the start.

00:29:14.792 --> 00:29:18.309
AG: So how do you discover the interest
of so many different parties?

00:29:18.333 --> 00:29:19.643
Just like with anchoring,

00:29:19.667 --> 00:29:22.309
you don't have to wait
for the other side to open up.

00:29:22.333 --> 00:29:24.476
If you start by talking
about your interests,

00:29:24.500 --> 00:29:25.976
you signal that you trust them

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:28.434
and the norm of reciprocity kicks in.

00:29:28.458 --> 00:29:30.792
That's when people are
more likely to share back.